add('scribe', 'LessonDraft', f"""Draft corpus/lessons/round-31.md (except `## Seat-reported failures`, drafted by another seat) as {D('lesson-round-31.md')}, modelled on {L}/corpus/lessons/round-30.md: title, author line (souji L1 SoujiR31; spot-check pending), frozen-contract paragraph, `## Gate` (start from {W1}/deliver-lesson-gate.md; rows for S222 ADMIT, the entry ADMIT, the held rows cited, per-entry REJECTs from {W1}/deliver-assim-sweep.md, `### SOURCES touched-row log (old -> new)` with the five used-by appends from `git -C {L} diff {BASE} {TIP} -- corpus/SOURCES.md`), `## Findings` (C1 MISSED 34->1 L29, C2 met, C3 met, amendments A0-A4 with the attacks that triggered them, M1), `## Mistakes` (class | evidence pointer | captured-by | fix: M1 rounds 26-28 uncarried seat failures, red 18/29/19 -> 0 in census/round-31/records/m1-red-before.txt and m1-after.txt; the L1's unquoted heredoc that dropped backticked spans from amendments.txt; the C1/C3 counters gameable at preregistration (cheapest-control rule) caught only by wave-1 critics; the preregistration's 23-vs-22 prose count), `## Receipts`, `## Residuals`. Every pointer must be a committed path (never a `.ufo/waves/` path). Read {R}/ for the records.""")
add('scribe', 'ScorecardLogDraft', f"""Draft, as {D('scorecard-log.md')}: (1) `### Round 31 measurements` for {L}/SCORECARD.md in the layout of `### Round 30 measurements` (C1 34->1 MISSED with both counter versions and records c1-before.txt, c1-after-v1.txt, c1-after-a4.txt; C2 base->after with c2-after-v1.txt/c2-after-v2.txt; C3 base->after with c3-after-*.txt; measured commits {C1L} {C2L} {C3L}); one sentence on owned scores; (2) `### Round 31 capability rows` (capability-cell binding audit; landing-gate reading precision; jj object-clock fixture) each naming a command that runs and its observed output from {R}/; (3) `### Planned (appended at round 31)` r32 bullet (residuals: L29, enumeration gap, gate blind spots, rounds 15/19/23/24/25 uncarried, /var/tmp in the gate); (4) a LOG.md entry in the style of the last entry of {L}/LOG.md. Never put a `| Lnn | SCORECARD.md:` row in it.""")
add('scribe', 'ReportDraft', f"""Draft the round report as {D('report-draft.md')} in the exact section order and house style of {F}/.ufo/reports/round-30/souji.md: Work performed (claims C1-C3 with verdicts; work items with commit hashes from `git -C {L} log --format='%H %s' {BASE}..{TIP}`), Landed changes (table), Before -> after measurements (per claim, counting command, records), Sources & frontier (rows 145->146 with the census count command, S222 added tier A, used-by touches, census start/end, assimilation line from {W1}/deliver-assim-sweep.md, considerthese absent, mined mistake, sourced claim C3), Trend verdicts (expansion/quality/discernment with evidence), SHONEN (one `[~]` line per box of {L}/SHONEN.md with a pointer that resolves), Other report lines. Leave the final lane hash and report-commit as `<final>` placeholders.""")
add('scribe', 'QualityRows', f"""Draft QUALITY.md rows Q67-Q69 for {L}/corpus/QUALITY.md as {D('quality-rows.md')}, starting from {W1}/deliver-quality-q67-q69.md and correcting them to what landed: Q67 capability-cell bindings (A2/A4 rules, the honest-miss rule for L29), Q68 landing-gate reading precision (fixture + SHIFT oracle; the letters-only prose limit), Q69 remover-subtraction for measured fixtures (A1 L13) and sentence-to-record spans (L10). Each row cites corpus/lessons/round-31.md and carries a runnable check copied from a command that ran this round. Also the matching SKILL.md `## Gate registry` rows for tools/souji-capability-cells.py, tests/fixtures/r31-landing-gate-precision.py and tests/fixtures/r31-jj-object-clock.sh.""")
add('simplifier', 'SpecHygiene2', f"""Validate this wave's spec hygiene: read {L}/.ufo/waves/round-31/make-spec-w2.py and the rendered {L}/.ufo/waves/round-31/w2-dispatch.json. Check distinct ids/prompts, allowed roles, flash roles (executor, scribe, critic, sentinel, revenger, simplifier) >= 50 % and attack roles (reviewer, critic, mutation-tester) >= 25 %, absolute paths, write scope limited to {W}/ and scratch under {SCR}/, no two items delivering the same file, no item that asks a seat to run the slow C1 counter concurrently with itself. Report defects with item ids.""")

c = collections.Counter(i['role'] for i in ITEMS)
n = len(ITEMS)
assert len({i['item'] for i in ITEMS}) == n and len({i['prompt'] for i in ITEMS}) == n
flash = sum(c[r] for r in ('executor', 'scribe', 'critic', 'sentinel', 'revenger', 'simplifier'))
attack = sum(c[r] for r in ('reviewer', 'critic', 'mutation-tester'))
assert 32 <= n <= 64 and flash * 2 >= n and attack * 4 >= n, (n, flash, attack)
spec = {'wave': 'souji-r31-w2', 'reportDir': '.ufo/waves/round-31/w2', 'maxLanes': 64, 'context': CONTEXT, 'items': ITEMS}
json.dump(spec, open(L + '/.ufo/waves/round-31/w2-spec.json', 'w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)
print(n, dict(c), 'flash', flash, 'attack', attack)
